<title>USA: ComEd Dresden nuke seen up later this week.</title>
<headline>ComEd Dresden nuke seen up later this week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Edison Co's 794 megawatt (MW) Dresden 3 nuclear power unit will likely restart later this week following Nuclear Regulatory Commission approval, the company said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We're still waiting for NRC approval (for changes to technical specifications). It will probably restart later this week,&quot; company spokesman Gary Wald said.</p>
<p>The unit, in Morris, Ill., was shut October 26 for maintenance.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit 2, with an identical generating capacity, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>ComEd is a subsidiary of Unicom Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
